## THE DONE RULE (C-79; quote it from the file, at write time, exactly)
The product owner's words, `CLARIFICATIONS.md:1714`: *"Done means merged to main, the same as Composer"*. **The test, `CLARIFICATIONS.md:1716` (C-79 `Settles:`), recorded there as the coordinator's reading of the ruling, not the product owner's words:** "a ticket moves to Done when its change is merged to main AND each Done-when clause of the ticket is MET; a clause that needs a deploy, a words approval or a further ruling is still not met by a merge ...; a merge alone never moves a ticket; the rule is silent on tickets whose work is done by a ruling or a measurement with no merged change ..., which stay as they are." The three conditions for a move (`CLARIFICATIONS.md:1727`, B1004 item 1), all required: (1) slot `DONE-SLOT` reads `MOVE-TO-DONE`; (2) your Done-when table (Step 4a) reads MET for every clause; (3) no gate or review line and no red run contradicts it. The readings you may use, each only as worded where it stands: (a), (b), (c), (d) at `:1727`; (e), (f), (g), (h) at `:1782` (B1019 item 1). Reading (d) as worded at `:1727`: "a residual that the landing comment files as another ticket does not by itself leave this ticket's clause unmet, unless the ticket's own acceptance names it". In Jira text the rule is cited as "the product owner's 2026-11-01 ruling that Done means merged to main", never by a card id.
**Reading (i), added for this batch (the coordinator's, not the product owner's; it rests on reading (d) and applies only where slot `CAP-READING` is YES):** a gate verdict of NO GO at the round cap whose open findings are each filed as ANOTHER ticket is not, by itself, "a gate or review line that contradicts" the move under condition (3), where every clause of this ticket's own Done-when reads MET at Step 4a and the ticket's own acceptance names none of the filed residuals. A residual recorded only as a comment ON this ticket is not filed as another ticket and holds it. It applies to MPSCALC-190, -191, -192, -193 (MPS #100: gate B547, NO GO round 2 of 2; B547-1, -2, -4 filed as MPSCALC-318, -319, -320) and MPSCALC-176 (MPS #125: gate B766, NO GO round 2 of 2 = THE CAP; B766-1 and -2 filed as MPSCALC-350, B766-3 as MPSCALC-351); it does NOT apply to MPSCALC-189 (B547-3 is comment 39958 on MPSCALC-189 itself) and is not used for MPSCALC-325 (Step 4a). PR #102's round-2 NO GO (gate B552) is not a cap verdict: a third round was allowed (C-55) and gate B575 gave GO WITH FINDINGS round 3 of 3.

